Fillets: patch 1140's end past the spine's end vertex wherever the edge's
faces go on meeting along its curve, and over pieces given up at the end
(mitcad#236).

The case: a rounding of 1 along a top's outline, round the outline's
corner (rounded with 2) up to the vertex V where a wall standing on the
top crosses the corner's rounding at a sharp vertical edge Eq. The
contact on the top runs onto the wall's foot already on the straight
edge before the corner: the analytic piece round the corner lies wholly
past the wall, and so does the straight piece's start, which is kept as
an extension with its top side given up. ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd took that
extension for the first piece, found no side whose contact leaves its
face and gave up; the corner then capped the straight piece's
prolongation with the wall, which it does not meet ("bouchon non
ecrit").

Now the pieces at the end with a side given up come before the first
piece on both faces, which is P; where the end is past V, the cut pieces
take their place (elsewhere such an end is left as before). And the end
past V (patch 1140) no longer needs Eq's faces tangent along it and the
face the contact leaves narrowing to a point at V: it needs Eq's curve
continued from V up to the end on both faces' surfaces (checked at four
points), which holds for faces tangent along Eq and for the wall and the
corner's cylinder running on along their vertical edge. The wall grows
down to the cut and Eq is prolonged down to the end, 1 below the top, as
in the file: on the stored design the boolean differences with the
file's body are empty both ways and the change of volume is 0.013 % off
the file's. Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_corners.cpp, a block lowered
on one side of a wall across its rounded corner, against the lower block
alone rounded on the far side of the wall's plane (failing without the
patch).
